          %p
            An analogous calculation shows that the counit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon \colon k[x]_{(x)} \to k
            is defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon(e_n(r)) = \delta_{0 n}
            (Kronecker delta).
          %p We summarize the calculations above as follows.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be an algebraically closed field. For each nonzero scalar
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(r)
              denote the
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mi x
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi r
                        %mi x
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_n(r) = \frac{(r x)^n}{(1 - r x)^{n+1}}
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x]_{(x)}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(e_n(r)) = \sum_{i+j=n} e_i(r) \otimes e_j(r), \qquad \varepsilon(e_n(r)) = \delta_{0 n}
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(0) = k[x]
              as a subspace of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x]_{(x)}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x]_{(x)}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi k
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x]_{(x)} \cong \bigoplus_{r \in k} L(r)
            %p
              according to the partial fraction decomposition of rational functions. Each of the coalgebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(r)
              is isomorphic to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x]
              with its standard coalgebra structure.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual concepts
              are those of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
